      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While resting in a dark room can sometimes help with eye fatigue, significant and sudden visual changes like flashes and floaters should never be treated as minor home issues. The lack of other symptoms does not eliminate the possibility of a serious underlying eye condition, such as a retinal tear. Because time is critical in managing these visual symptoms, please prioritize having a healthcare professional examine your eye as soon as possible.",
      "source": "target",
